{"extract": "Michalis Chrisochoidis (Greek: Μιχάλης Χρυσοχοΐδης, born 31 October 1955) is a Greek politician and member of the Hellenic Parliament for the Athens B2 constituency with New Democracy. He currently serves as Minister for Citizen Protection in the Second Cabinet of Kyriakos Mitsotakis. He had served in the same role on four occasions (1999–2003, 2009–2010, 2012 and 2019–2021), as a member of PASOK and an independent politician. He has also served as Minister for the Economy, Competitiveness and Shipping (2010), Minister for Regional Development and Competitiveness (2010–2011), Minister for Development, Competitiveness and Shipping (2011–2012), Minister for Infrastructure, Transport and Networks (2013–2015) and Minister for Health (2023–2024).", "links": [{"ns": 10, "title": "Template:Infobox officeholder", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Adonis Georgiadis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Anna Diamantopoulou", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Antonis Samaras", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Athens B2", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Christos Papoutsis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Costas Simitis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Eleftherios Oikonomou", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Filippos Petsalnikos", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "George Papandreou", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Giorgos Floridis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Giorgos Stathakis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Greece", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Greek language", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Hellenic Parliament", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Imathia", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Incumbent", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Independent politician", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kingdom of Greece", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kostis Hatzidakis", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kyriakos Mitsotakis", "exists